<p>And here's the thing about fall on the Gulf Coast that people from up north don't realize: it's still summer weather. October averages 84&deg;F. The Gulf water temperature stays in the low 80s through mid-November. The rain is slightly more frequent than spring but comes in 20-minute afternoon bursts, not all-day washouts. You get the beach to yourself by 9am because there's nobody here.</p>

<div class="callout">
    <strong>The sweet spot:</strong> Late October through mid-November. Rates at their lowest &mdash; sub-$500/night average, 27% below peak season pricing. Temps in the low 80s, hurricane season winding down, and zero spring-break crowds. The Bradenton-area restaurants are half-empty &mdash; you'll get a table at Star Fish Company without the 90-minute wait.
</div>

<p>The one catch with summer? It's genuinely hot. 90&deg;F with Florida humidity means you'll want a pool at the rental (all 5 of our properties have one), and you'll plan beach time for mornings. But summer also brings families on school break, so it's still a popular travel season &mdash; just not as pricey as the snowbird months.</p>


<h2>Transportation: Fly Into SRQ, Not TPA</h2>

<p>Quick math that saves $100+ per trip.</p>

<p>Tampa International (TPA) is the big airport. Everyone defaults to it. The Uber from TPA to Bradenton runs about $76. To Anna Maria Island, $65&ndash;$100 depending on traffic and surge pricing.</p>

<p>Sarasota-Bradenton International (SRQ) is 16 miles from AMI. The Uber to Anna Maria Island costs $26&ndash;$30. To Bradenton, $20&ndash;$25. SRQ has expanded significantly &mdash; Allegiant, Southwest, JetBlue, Delta, United, and American all fly in now. The terminal is small enough that you're at baggage claim 10 minutes after landing.</p>

<p>The flight into SRQ might cost $20&ndash;$50 more than TPA on some routes. But you save $50&ndash;$70 on ground transportation <em>each way</em>, plus 30&ndash;45 minutes in the car. For a family, the SRQ math almost always wins.</p>

<p>If you do need a rental car (and you probably do, unless you're staying on AMI and using the trolley), SRQ rates run $27&ndash;$40/day. TPA averages $35&ndash;$49/day for the same vehicle class because of higher airport fees.</p>

